<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Insect mamono mourn their own like drones, not like daughters (user ruling
		2026-09-27: "a greatly lowered mood debuff for killed colonists, to match
		the disposable nature of insect momos").

		The lever is vanilla's own: `ThoughtDef.nullifyingGenes` is read by
		ThoughtUtility.NullifyingGene and through ThoughtUtility.ThoughtNullified,
		which Thought_Memory.MoodOffset calls first thing - so a listed gene makes
		the memory worth nothing, and the mood screen never shows the line. It is
		the same list that already carries `Psychopath` as a nullifying TRAIT on
		ColonistLost.

		That switch cannot scale: there is no XML dial between the full hit and no
		hit. So the list below is exactly the heavy half of grief - a dead child,
		spouse, fiance, lover, sibling or grandchild, and a close friend at -10 or
		worse. Left alone on purpose: her parents and extended kin (-4 to -8),
		bonded animals (-8), and the colony's own generic losses - KnowColonistDied
		at -3 and ColonistLost at -6 - which are the token that keeps a dead
		colonist costing her something.

		Both files are covered because vanilla splits the two ways a colonist can be
		gone (Died = died on the map, Lost = gone from it) and they mirror each
		other def for def.

		PMM_Gene_Insect is the shared insect gene, so this is one patch for every
		insect caste, and it covers a woman transformed into one at runtime too.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="PawnWithGoodOpinionDied" or defName="MySonDied" or defName="MyDaughterDied" or defName="MyHusbandDied" or defName="MyWifeDied" or defName="MyFianceDied" or defName="MyFianceeDied" or defName="MyLoverDied" or defName="MyBrotherDied" or defName="MySisterDied" or defName="MyGrandchildDied"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<nullifyingGenes>
				<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			</nullifyingGenes>
		</value>
	</Operation>
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
		<xpath>Defs/ThoughtDef[defName="PawnWithGoodOpinionLost" or defName="MySonLost" or defName="MyDaughterLost" or defName="MyHusbandLost" or defName="MyWifeLost" or defName="MyFianceLost" or defName="MyFianceeLost" or defName="MyLoverLost" or defName="MyBrotherLost" or defName="MySisterLost" or defName="MyGrandchildLost"]</xpath>
		<value>
			<nullifyingGenes>
				<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			</nullifyingGenes>
		</value>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
